From 6be18ded4dfb97dda2b8cbc26e0b916e60f6bdf3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 05:16:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] NOTE-KEYGATE: the alarm note's on-screen keys follow golden's
 key lock -- an IC fallen into the test site (open the Index door, press Z1),
 contact over, auto-clean door, clean pad, safe lock, index jam door,
 auto-retest door refuse the press, as the physical keys already did

The every-component check (helper motorB) found that the web answer path (tools/wb_serve.cpp modal.answer / dialog.response)
accepted SKIP / RETRY / TRAY FEED / TRAY END / CLEAN OUT / HOME / TRAIN / ONE CYCLE whatever the machine state, while golden V906
note.cpp:2843-2870 TfNote::BtnSkipClick (those 8 keys' OnClick, note.dfm) + UpdateButtonStatus :2764-2873 ignore the press. So the
screen could RETRY + START with an IC still in the socket. The physical panel keys (W906_AlarmIoAnswer) already had the lock.

* forms/fNote_WebKeyGate.cpp (new, ht9045_sm): W906_NoteWebKeyGate(bOpenChamberDoor, why) -- the golden conditions, each with a reason
  (golden only ignores the press; the web needs the reason). Not ported members stay as the panel path treats them
  (iICFloattingCheckStep = 0, bOpenSixDoor = false).
* tools/wb_serve.cpp: the gate runs for every key but RESET (BtnResetClick, whose main half is not wired) on the line before the
  D-026 password gate -- golden: a locked key cannot be chosen, so DoPassword never runs for it (and that gate uses up the one-shot
  pass); refused = CompleteCommand(false, reason) and the wait goes on. W906_AlarmIoAnswer shares its bOpenChamberDoor (TfNote
  member, golden Timer1Timer :3187-3205) through g_w906NoteChamberDoorPtr, like g_w906NoteSelPtr. All line-neutral.
* tests/test_note_webkeygate.cpp (ctest NoteWebKeyGate, 13 checks): each condition refuses with its reason and passes when cleared;
  CC_SCK exempt; source pins (gate before the D-026 gate, the shared flag, the IC-fall arm).

Verified: o2 wb_serve 0 errors; ctest NoteWebKeyGate 13/13, D026_NoteAuth (its source pin on the next line intact),
WB_DialogMailbox, MainCloseStop, WebCmdGuard 5/5; PE 80/80; production_audit 0 changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
